# Marklower - the inline markup of a chunk. From MARKLOWER.md.
Marklower
description: inline-only prose; tables and lists are yamlover nodes
- >
  **Marklower** is yamlover's prose format: a markup language deliberately a notch *below* Markdown
  (hence the name). It is the format a **chapter's chunks** carry - `$defs/chunk` declares
  `format: text/marklower` and schema propagation stamps every prose chunk with it, so an article
  needs no per-chunk tag ([chapters](*::documents:chapter)). It is asked for by name: a format-less
  string *elsewhere* in the tree is data, not prose. This part defines the language AND the
  structures it delegates to - [tables](*::documents:marklower:tables), [lists](*::documents:marklower:lists),
  and [embeds](*::documents:marklower:embeds).
  Companion language material: the [pointer grammar](*::language:pointers), the [type
  lattice](*::language:model), the [schema vocabulary](*::meta).
